,title,link,text,language,family
0,Hawu language - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hawu_language,"The Hawu language (Hawu: Lii Hawu) is the language of the Savu people of Savu Island in Indonesia and of Raijua Island off the western tip of Savu. Hawu has been referred to by a variety of names such as Havu, Savu, Sabu, Sawu, and is known to outsiders as Savu or Sabu (thus Havunese, Savunese, Sawunese). [2][3] Hawu belongs to the Malayo-Polynesian branch of the Austronesian language family ...",Hawu,Austronesian
1,Taiwanese Indigenous pop music - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Taiwanese_Indigenous_pop_music,"Taiwanese Indigenous pop music comprises contemporary songs performed in Austronesian languages native to Taiwan, blending modern pop music with Indigenous linguistic and cultural elements. It has steadily gained mainstream recognition over the past two decades, reflecting a broader cultural revival and renewed pride among Taiwanese indigenous peoples. The music fosters inter-ethnic dialogue ...",Hawu,Austronesian
2,Hawu - YouTube Music,https://music.youtube.com/playlist?list=PLhenevJSR1qKJIddamSYTP4KHuPtG0YE-,"Hawu Sigiya ngengoma Sign in to create & share playlists, get personalized recommendations, and more.",Hawu,Austronesian
3,hawu - YouTube Music,https://music.youtube.com/playlist?list=PLAgMIJNwLMETLMwqWa6qveRyfdpbsEeKu,"Listen to hawu on YouTube Music - a dedicated music app with official songs, music videos, remixes, covers, and more.",Hawu,Austronesian
4,Hawu language — Grokipedia,https://grokipedia.com/page/hawu_language,"Hawu (Hawu: Lii Hawu), also known as Savu, Sawu, or Sabu, is an Austronesian language spoken primarily by the Savu people on Savu Island and the nearby island of Raijua in the Sabu Sea, off the western coast of Timor in Indonesia's East Nusa Tenggara province. [1][2] With approximately 95,000 speakers (2023), it serves as a stable indigenous ...",Hawu,Austronesian
5,Austronesian Soundscapes: Performing Arts in Oceania and ... - JSTOR,https://www.jstor.org/stable/j.ctt46mvnd,"Austronesian Soundscapes is a collection of essays on Austronesian musics that transcends disciplinary frontiers in the humanities and social sciences. In all of Austronesia, music plays a crucial role in the negotiation of cultural identities; yet research on the diversity of the Austronesian cultural belt's music has hitherto been rather sparse.",Hawu,Austronesian
6,Austronesian Music - Music genre - Rate Your Music,https://rateyourmusic.com/genre/austronesian-music/,"Austronesian music nowadays refers to the ongoing evolution and fusion of various cultural influences from foreign and neighbouring cultures. These influences have over the centuries introduced new instruments, styles, and genres, blending age-old elements with newer traditions.",Hawu,Austronesian
7,Musical aspects of Austronesian culture - Academia.edu,https://www.academia.edu/4175401/Musical_aspects_of_Austronesian_culture,"Musical practices are often overlooked in cultural history, yet they reveal significant connections to the Austronesian cultural expansion across the Indo-Pacific region. By examining specific musical examples like polyphonic singing, various instruments, and dance forms, the study highlights the distinct characteristics of musical traditions in Taiwan compared to those in mainland regions and ...",Hawu,Austronesian
8,Austronesian Music - Melodigging,https://www.melodigging.com/genre/austronesian-music,"Austronesian music is an umbrella term for the diverse musical traditions of Austronesian-speaking peoples, whose homelands stretch from Taiwan through Island Southeast Asia to Oceania and Madagascar.",Hawu,Austronesian
9,Taxonomies of Taiwanese Aboriginal Musical Instruments,https://ourarchive.otago.ac.nz/esploro/outputs/doctoral/Taxonomies-of-Taiwanese-Aboriginal-Musical-Instruments/9926480150701891,"This investigation also makes original contributions to extend the instrument type and the numerical entry of the Hornbostel-Sachs system of musical instrument classification. Moreover, this dissertation provides a link between Taiwanese aboriginal instruments and other Austronesian musical instruments.",Hawu,Austronesian
